# Monterey cypress, sheared form: Monterey cypress on a sea cliff: a smooth, dense crown with a flat, thin top over bare, twisting limbs, sheared by the wind, about 2.5 times wider than tall.
# Foliage pads at the limb ends (Branch Base), lying almost flat (Leaf Face Up, Leaf Face Up Variation), an
# umbrella envelope with a flat top, the wind toward -Y (Wind Direction, Wind Shear, Wind Bend). Measured
# against Point Lobos and Monterey photos (Wikimedia Commons). In use the trunk leans 6 degrees downwind
# (a rotation of the whole tree) and the leaves carry a drawn foliage-pad texture.

